# React 19 rules

Apply this rule to React 19+ components. Confirm the repository’s React version and whether the React Compiler is enabled before making compiler-specific assumptions.

- `ref` is a normal prop now. Do NOT use `forwardRef` in new components.
- When the React Compiler is enabled, do NOT hand-wrap things in `useMemo`, `useCallback`, or `React.memo` unless profiling shows a real regression. When it is not enabled, profile before adding manual memoization rather than adding it by habit.
- Mutations go through `<form action={fn}>` + `useActionState` (from `react`) when using React form actions. Never introduce `useFormState` from `react-dom`.
- Compute derived values during render. `useEffect` is for external systems only, not for deriving state from props or other state.

References:
- React 19 release: https://react.dev/blog/2024/12/05/react-19
- `ref` and `forwardRef`: https://react.dev/reference/react/forwardRef
- `useActionState`: https://react.dev/reference/react/useActionState
- React Compiler and manual memoization: https://react.dev/reference/react/useMemo
